Observability, Telemetry & System Health
Version 1.0
Status: Implementation Architecture Specification
System: OneDraft CAD-AI Platform
Primary Intelligence: Aria Powered
Scope: Platform Observability, Telemetry, Diagnostics, Monitoring and System Health
Dependencies: OneDraft Stacks 1.0–29.0
Architectural Position: Operational Systems Layer

1. PURPOSE
The OneDraft platform has now established its foundational project model, computational geometry system, regulatory and compliance engine, validation framework, documentation engine, review and acceptance workflow, runtime orchestration, asynchronous job system, artifact storage, integration/event architecture, and identity/security boundary.
The next requirement is the ability to continuously determine whether those systems are operating correctly.
OneDraft therefore requires a dedicated observability architecture.
The Observability, Telemetry & System Health subsystem provides the instrumentation necessary to determine:
what the system is doing
what the system has done
whether the system is functioning correctly
where a failure occurred
which project or operation was affected
which version of the model was involved
which service performed the operation
how long the operation required
whether downstream artifacts remain trustworthy
whether the system requires intervention
Observability becomes part of the OneDraft operational system of record.

2. OBSERVABILITY PRINCIPLE
OneDraft shall not depend upon individual service logs as its sole mechanism of system diagnosis.
The platform shall produce structured telemetry across:
CLIENT
 ↓
API GATEWAY
 ↓
IDENTITY / AUTHORIZATION
 ↓
DOMAIN SERVICES
 ↓
ARIA
 ↓
COMMAND SYSTEM
 ↓
GEOMETRY ENGINE
 ↓
COMPLIANCE ENGINE
 ↓
VALIDATION ENGINE
 ↓
DOCUMENTATION ENGINE
 ↓
ARTIFACT STORAGE
 ↓
JOB / WORKER SYSTEM
 ↓
EVENT BUS
 ↓
DATABASE
Each major operation must be traceable across the participating services.
The objective is not merely to record errors.
The objective is to establish causal operational visibility.

3. THREE PRIMARY TELEMETRY SIGNALS
OneDraft observability shall initially use three primary telemetry classes:
LOGS
METRICS
TRACES
These signals are complementary.
Logs explain:
what happened
Metrics explain:
how often and how much
Traces explain:
where the operation travelled through the system

4. FOURTH SIGNAL — SYSTEM EVENTS
Operational telemetry shall remain distinct from domain events.
Domain events describe changes to the OneDraft computational system.
Operational telemetry describes the behaviour of the software executing those changes.
For example:
DOMAIN EVENT
REVISION_CREATED
is distinct from:
OPERATIONAL EVENT
revision_service.create_revision.duration = 182ms
This distinction prevents operational diagnostics from contaminating the project domain model.

