17. LIVENESS
Liveness determines whether the process itself is functioning.
Example:
GET /health/live
A liveness failure indicates that the process may need restart or replacement.

18. READINESS
Readiness determines whether the service can accept work.
Example:
GET /health/ready
Readiness may depend upon:
database connectivity
required service availability
configuration validity
queue connectivity
required runtime dependencies

19. DEPENDENCY HEALTH
Services shall be capable of reporting dependency state.
Example:
PostgreSQL      READY
Event Bus       READY
Object Storage  READY
Job Queue       READY
Telemetry       READY
A service may remain alive while being unavailable for normal work.

